{"seq":1235,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"overlapping-outcomes","severity":"serious","evidence":"Annual transit is at least 1,825,000,000 barrels but below the article’s full-year pace range implied by its estimate (whose upper end is 3,650,000,000 barrels).","rule":"PRD 06 ladder rule; split_seven_day_poc.py META_SYSTEM requires mutually exclusive outcomes.","mechanism":"In 1235.json, the next outcome has the same bounds. The prototype rejects the ladder and writes v76 with no outcomes or judgement."}
{"seq":1235,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"wrong-subject","severity":"serious","evidence":"\"object\": \"new\", \"new_subject\": \"Strait of Hormuz crude oil transit\"","rule":"split-v2-design.md §3 requires choosing a listed subject when one fits.","mechanism":"In 1235.json, record preparation creates a new subject instead of using the existing middle-east-conflict subject, fragmenting related research."}
{"seq":1239,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"reversed-revenue-outcomes","severity":"blocker","evidence":"\"label\": \"Strongly bullish\", \"condition\": \"FY2026 total revenue is below 7011000000 USD, more than 5% below the latest reported trailing-twelve-month revenue of 7380000000 USD.\"","rule":"split_seven_day_poc.py META_SYSTEM requires company outcomes to run from strongly bullish to strongly bearish according to what is good or bad for the business.","mechanism":"In 1239.json, record preparation reverses the direction: the lowest revenue is strongly bullish and the highest is strongly bearish. The checks accept and the writer stores it."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"B","class":"unrelated-company-filing","severity":"serious","evidence":"The same Q2 2026 data set shows that Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing generated NT$1.2 trillion in second-quarter revenue, up 36 percent year over year from its Q2 2025 base","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and §5.3: another company's figures need an identifiable demand, supply, competition or pricing path to the question.","mechanism":"In 1240.json, B files TSMC revenue, employee bonuses and operating profit under v78, ON Semiconductor's revenue question, without establishing such a path. The broad revenue fallback is a likely contributor; the trace does not prove the model's reason."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"judging","class":"growth-applied-twice","severity":"blocker","evidence":"Carrying the reported 36% year-over-year growth forward implies about NT$6.53 trillion (NT$4.8T × 1.36)","rule":"Signed standard §7 and D218 require the reasoning to distinguish source evidence from inference and support the conclusion.","mechanism":"In 1240.json, v79 annualizes a quarter that already includes the 36% year-over-year growth, then multiplies that current pace by the same growth again. This selects the highest outcome on an unsupported calculation. judging-v7 asks for growth to be carried forward but does not distinguish past year-over-year growth from prospective growth."}
{"seq":1246,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-narrower-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"Management continues to see around $20 billion in total server CPU demand and preliminarily expects CPU revenue to more than double in fiscal 2028.","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and D207: file evidence under the narrowest existing question it informs.","mechanism":"In 1246.json, B links this CPU-specific forecast only to v72, total revenue, while v7 already tracks stand-alone CPU revenue. The broad fallback can send specific evidence to total revenue."}
{"seq":1249,"lane":"judging","class":"lower-bound-treated-as-point","severity":"serious","evidence":"The reference is the article’s forecast of more than $200 billion, corresponding to rung 3’s $200 billion–below $250 billion band.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 requires preserving a statement's limits; §7 and D218 require a conclusion to be supported by the evidence.","mechanism":"In 1249.json, v80 places an open-ended estimate in a bounded outcome despite acknowledging that the source supplies no upper bound. The record-preparation reference and judging both treat the floor as though it were a central estimate."}
{"seq":1250,"lane":"matching","class":"different-populations-merged","severity":"serious","evidence":"How much will the five top hyperscalers spend on capital expenditures in calendar 2027?","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 requires preserving the population; D197 uses theme, measure and period as the identity key.","mechanism":"In 1250.json, matching records \"shared quantity: merge by key (D197)\" into v5, which asks for four hyperscalers' data-center spending. The key discards the population difference, so the five-company forecast is presented under a four-company question."}
{"seq":1251,"lane":"A","class":"unverifiable-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"What share of NVIDIA’s FY2028 revenue will come from customers it has financed in some way?","rule":"Signed standard §4 requires an outcome that can be checked against public material on a date.","mechanism":"In 1251.json, A assumes the annual report will disclose this broad customer category and its revenue share; the article provides a forecast but no evidence that the realized share will be publicly reported. v81 is opened on that unverified check."}
{"seq":1251,"lane":"A","class":"customer-revenue-misstated-as-financing","severity":"serious","evidence":"Since the company's revenue could top $670 billion next year, around $168 billion could be funded by its own balance sheet.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4: preserve what a figure measures and its conditions; unsupported conclusions cannot be represented as source facts.","mechanism":"In 1251.json, the opening passage and summary accept the author's conversion of revenue from financed customers into revenue funded by NVIDIA. The 25% customer-revenue share does not establish the amount NVIDIA finances."}
{"seq":1252,"lane":"A","class":"missing-product-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"CEO Elon Musk said early this year that the electric vehicle company could be mass-manufacturing and selling its humanoid assistants by the end of 2027","rule":"Signed standard §3 B and §4: a principal product milestone that can affect positioning and be publicly checked may open when no existing question covers it.","mechanism":"In 1252.json, A opens a question about another company's market share but proposes no question about the stated commercialization milestone. The reason for the omission is not established by the trace."}
{"seq":1253,"lane":"judging","class":"lower-bound-treated-as-point","severity":"serious","evidence":"The guidance supports revenue above $40 billion, but does not quantify growth beyond doubling enough to imply at least $45 billion.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 requires preserving a statement's limits; §7 and D218 require a conclusion to be supported by the evidence.","mechanism":"In 1253.json, v83 chooses the $40–45 billion outcome even though 'more than double' also permits every higher outcome. Neither the preparation reference nor the judgement supplies a basis for the upper boundary."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"A","class":"background-kept-as-evidence","severity":"minor","evidence":"An AI cloud is an emerging kind of intermediary, one that buys Nvidia's chips, packs them into clusters, and leases capacity to companies that never need to negotiate with a chip designer directly.","rule":"Signed standard §5.3 excludes general background and descriptions of existing arrangements without a new action.","mechanism":"In 1254.json, A includes an explanation of the business model as evidence for v84. Its closing review retains context that does not itself report a new development."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"wrong-original-attribution","severity":"serious","evidence":"\"original_who\": \"Adam Spatacco\", \"original_day\": \"2026-08-30\", \"tier\": \"fact\"","rule":"Signed standard §5.4: record the original speaker and original date; when the original date is unknown, leave it unknown.","mechanism":"In 1254.json, record preparation attributes the reported quarterly company figures to the article author and uses the article date as their original date, even though A describes the author as reporting NVIDIA's results."}
{"seq":1254,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"The AI Clouds, Industrial, and Enterprise group (ACIE) generated $40.3 billion, an increase of 25% from last quarter and 138% year over year.","rule":"Signed standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one record; a record can link to the relevant questions.","mechanism":"In 1254.json, A passes the customer-group figures as e1 for v84 and B passes the same ACIE figures as e7 for v10. Both survive the handover as separate records, with different original attribution."}
{"summary":{"items_read":26,"incomplete_review":[1234,1235,1237,1238,1239,1240,1241,1243,1244,1245,1246,1247,1248,1249,1250,1251,1252,1253,1254,1256],"limitation":"The articles and extracted outputs were read, but the full matching reasons and all downstream ledger links and cited evidence were not exhaustively checked for these items. The findings are therefore not a complete census.","classes":{"overlapping-outcomes":1,"wrong-subject":1,"reversed-revenue-outcomes":1,"unrelated-company-filing":1,"growth-applied-twice":1,"wrong-narrower-question":1,"lower-bound-treated-as-point":2,"different-populations-merged":1,"unverifiable-question":1,"customer-revenue-misstated-as-financing":1,"missing-product-question":1,"background-kept-as-evidence":1,"wrong-original-attribution":1,"same-article-evidence-duplicated":1}}}